{"name":"Tragic Juliet","hex":"#927383","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tragic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Causing great sadness or suffering.","Relating to tragedy in a literary work."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An obsessive fan, a superfan","A writer of tragedy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tragic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tragedy","blocks":[{"text":"A tragedy is a genre of drama based on human suffering, specifically by way of terrible or sorrowful events that befall a main character or cast of characters. Traditionally, the intention of tragedy is to invoke an accompanying catharsis, or a \"pain [that] awakens pleasure,\" for the audience. While many cultures have developed forms that provoke this paradoxical response, the term tragedy often refers to a specific tradition of drama that has played a unique and important role historically in the self-definition of Western civilization. That tradition has been multiple and discontinuous, yet the term has often been used to invoke a powerful effect of cultural identity and historical continuity—\"the Greeks and the Elizabethans, in one cultural form; Hellenes and Christians, in a common activity,\" as Raymond Williams puts it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Reliefs_from_Tarentum_%28Berlin_Ant_Sk_1641%2C_1642%29.jpg/330px-Reliefs_from_Tarentum_%28Berlin_Ant_Sk_1641%2C_1642%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tragedy"},{"title":"Juliet","blocks":[{"text":"Juliet Capulet is the female protagonist in William Shakespeare's romantic tragedy Romeo and Juliet. A 13-year-old girl, Juliet is the only daughter of the patriarch of the House of Capulet. She falls in love with the male protagonist Romeo, a member of the House of Montague, with which the Capulets have a blood feud. The story has a long history that precedes Shakespeare himself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg/330px-Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juliet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png/500px-Books_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABooks_and_Scroll_Ornament_with_Open_Book.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg/500px-Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg/1280px-Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg/500px-Pompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bacchae, ancient Greek tragedy by Euripides","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APompeii_-_Casa_dei_Vettii_-_Pentheus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Pompeii_-_Casa_del_Centenario_-_Orest.jpg/500px-Pompeii_-_Casa_del_Centenario_-_Orest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Pompeii_-_Casa_d